# Brainstorming and Ideation Phase

## Project Name

Script-Controlled ACL – Restrict Record Access Based on Field Value

## Project Idea

The main idea of this project is to implement a Script-Controlled Access Control List (ACL) in ServiceNow.

The ACL is used to restrict users from viewing records unless they meet the required conditions.

In this project, access to records is controlled using user roles and the value of the Branch field.

## Problem Statement

In a ServiceNow application, different users may have different access requirements.

Unauthorized users should not be allowed to view, create, modify, or delete records.

Therefore, an access control mechanism is required to protect records and provide access only to authorized users.

## Proposed Solution

The proposed solution is to create a custom Institution Details table in ServiceNow and apply Access Control Lists to control different operations.

The project uses:

- User roles
- Branch field conditions
- Script-controlled ACL
- READ ACL
- CREATE ACL
- WRITE ACL
- DELETE ACL

## Main Objective

The main objective of the project is to demonstrate how Script-Controlled ACLs can provide record-level security in ServiceNow.

The project aims to:

- Restrict unauthorized access to records.
- Control access using user roles.
- Restrict READ access based on the Branch field.
- Control CREATE access.
- Control WRITE access.
- Control DELETE access.
- Provide full access to administrators.

## User and Role Idea

A test user named EEE User is created for the project.

The following roles are planned:

- bb1 – READ access
- bb2 – CREATE access
- bb3 – WRITE access
- bb4 – DELETE access

All the required roles are assigned to the EEE User.

## Table Idea

A custom table named Institution Details is planned for storing student-related information.

Table Name:

u_institution_details

The table contains fields such as:

- Student Roll Number
- Student Name
- Faculty Name
- Branch
- Email
- Phone Number
- Description

## Branch-Based Access Idea

The Branch field is planned with the following values:

- ECE
- EEE
- CSE

Different branch values are used to test record-level access.

The READ ACL uses the condition that the Branch is EEE.

Users with the required access can view the permitted records, while unauthorized users are restricted.

## ACL Idea

The project is planned with four main ACL operations.

### READ ACL

The READ ACL controls whether users can view records.

Role:

bb1

Condition:

Branch is EEE

The READ ACL also uses a script to control access.

### CREATE ACL

The CREATE ACL controls the creation of new records.

Role:

bb2

### WRITE ACL

The WRITE ACL controls modification of existing records.

Role:

bb3

### DELETE ACL

The DELETE ACL controls deletion of records.

Role:

bb4

## Security Idea

The project focuses on protecting records from unauthorized access.

The ACL evaluates the user's role and the required conditions before allowing access.

Administrators retain full access to the records.

## Expected Benefits

- Provides record-level security.
- Restricts unauthorized users.
- Provides role-based access control.
- Provides condition-based access control.
- Controls READ, CREATE, WRITE, and DELETE operations.
- Helps protect sensitive records.
- Provides practical understanding of ServiceNow ACLs.

## Expected Outcome

The expected outcome is a ServiceNow implementation where access to Institution Details records is controlled using Script-Controlled ACLs.

The project demonstrates how user roles and record field values can be used together to control access.

## Conclusion

The Brainstorming and Ideation phase identifies the need for secure record access in ServiceNow.

The proposed project uses Script-Controlled ACLs to control READ, CREATE, WRITE, and DELETE operations.

The idea will be implemented and tested in the following project phases.
